screens.layout:
SKY MODE
- A full-bleed night sky with the aurora along the bottom.
- Every live session is a star, grouped into a named constellation per project folder. Stars in the same repository are joined by faint lines.
- The Mac is the moon at the top-right: battery %, lid state, keep-awake on/off, and a cutoff arc.
- The dispatcher line at the top: '7 sessions · 3 projects · 2 workflows'.
- Star encoding (every attribute is a real signal):
  - brightness = tool calls per minute;
  - colour = state (teal working, amber needs you, dim white idle);
  - a slow halo with satellite dots = a workflow, with one dot filling per finished agent ('4 of 7');
  - a dashed amber orbit = stuck;
  - a hollow star with a hairline countdown = rate-limited;
  - a grey dimmed star with a horizon tick = paused at the battery cutoff.

LANES MODE (graft from Handover's Fleet)
- An accessible list, one row per session, grouped by project and ordered needs-you → working → idle.
- Each row: star glyph, title (the first prompt, editable), last action in mono, and a 4-hour activity strip. Its states:
  - bright teal line = working;
  - dotted = idle;
  - amber node = waiting;
  - jagged amber = stuck;
  - a gap with a reset time = rate-limited;
  - a grey band = battery pause.
- Workflows show as braided sub-lanes.
- With several paired Macs, non-live Macs appear as dimmed 'standby' groups with 'Make live'.

TOGGLE
- A bottom-centre glass segment above the capsule switches between Sky and Lanes.

HEADER
- A large star with the session's own pulse, project / branch / agent, and the state sentence ('Working · 14 tool calls this turn · 6 m').
- 'Stop' as a text button.

LENS CONTROL
- A glass segmented control: Story · Screen · Changes · Workflows. Workflows appears only if the session has workflows.
- The default lens is Screen when the session is waiting, Changes when opened from a Review card, and Story otherwise.

LENSES
- STORY:
  - the transcript as a readable thread;
  - your instructions as right-aligned bubbles stamped 'from iPhone 14:02';
  - turn summaries on the left;
  - long tool output collapsed;
  - pending prompts pinned inline as the same decision card used in Now;
  - answered asks collapsed to receipts;
  - battery-pause and rate-limit dividers.
  - From v4.1, earlier Claude sessions in the same project folder load as you scroll up, with 'Session started 09:12' dividers. This needs a new relay request to read transcripts already on the Mac's disk.
- SCREEN:
  - the live terminal mirror, end-to-end encrypted, in SF Mono on dark glass, auto-following;
  - a status bar ('cmux › pane 3 · updated 1 s ago · live dot');
  - a key row labelled by meaning in the current state: 'Esc = Deny', '1 = Approve', Enter, ↑, ↓.
- CHANGES:
  - the what-changed file list with +/− counts and the test result, then a tap-through unified diff.
  - In Review mode an action bar is pinned at the bottom: 'Looks good', 'Ask for changes', 'Carry on' and 'Stop'.
- WORKFLOWS:
  - the multi-agent run as a ring of agent nodes ('4 of 7 · 11 m'). Tap a node for that agent's transcript.

COMPOSER (pinned)
- Its mode chip changes with the session state:
  - busy: 'Steer · will queue after this step', plus Stop;
  - waiting: locked, showing Approve / Deny / 'Tell it instead (Esc first)';
  - idle: 'Next task'.
- Standing-reply chips: 'Carry on', 'Run the tests, then stop', 'Summarise what you did', 'Stop and explain what's failing'.
